<title>AUSTRIA: Austria FinMin says considers another bank sale.</title>
<headline>Austria FinMin says considers another bank sale.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Finance Minister Viktor Klima said on Thursday he was not sure whether revenues from the planned sale of Creditanstalt would be realised before year-end, possibly resulting in the need for additional revenues.</p>
<p>Klima told Austrian radio he may consider selling &quot;another&quot; bank in order to keep the budget deficit at its projected level.</p>
<p>&quot;We will certainly make a decision on Creditanstalt this year, but it is not sure whether the money will flow (this year),&quot; he said. &quot;We have budgeted for another sale to close this gap.&quot; Asked which sale he was considering, he said: &quot;We're also taking about a bank.&quot;</p>
</text>
